{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01HshSSJ2JLN9fPcbn2SvpTu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AbHcSFY526tVu1DtCM92bP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='TODO.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace('- [ ] **sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic**', '- [x] **sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic**')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nwith open('KEY_DECISIONS.md','a') as f:\n    f.write(\"\"\"\n- sos_1: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined and used by several FDN cards but\n  **never fired** by `declare_attackers_step` — fired it there (after all\n  attackers are declared, rule 508.3a) as a small additive engine fix.\n- sos_1: \"exile it instead\" needs replacement effects on a *stack → graveyard*\n  move, which `move_to_zone` only consulted for battlefield-leaving moves.\n  Added `SpellGoesToGraveyardReplacementEvent`, passed it from\n  `_resolve_spell`'s instant/sorcery branch, and widened the `move_to_zone`\n  gate to also consult replacements for stack moves. The card registers a\n  one-shot replacement keyed to the specific free-cast spell.\n- sos_1: countered free-cast spells bypass the replacement (fdn_48-style local\n  `_counter_spell` moves the card directly) — deliberate limitation; the\n  oracle \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard\" is honored on the\n  resolution path.\n\"\"\")\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"sos_1: The Dawning Archaic\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Mark sos_1 done, log decisions, commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":989,"cache_read_input_tokens":160376,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":989},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98b35815-b35f-4b80-bf9f-66c04f25a22f","