{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_016EGfq4eEQgamjapFqzfrHt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BoEkpJxzsspo2JXXtg5DXS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='TODO.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace('- [ ] **sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex**', '- [x] **sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex**')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nwith open('KEY_DECISIONS.md','a') as f:\n    f.write(\"\"\"\n- sos_257: restricted mana lives in a separate `ManaPool._restricted` bucket\n  supporting exactly one restriction kind (\"instant_or_sorcery\") — commented\n  as a deliberate limitation, no general predicate system. `can_pay`/`pay`\n  gained an optional `spell=` kwarg (passed from `cast_spell`); restricted\n  mana is spent before unrestricted mana of the same type.\n- sos_257: the {5} animation has no printed duration, so it is permanent —\n  implemented as in-place mutation that also updates `_original_card_types`\n  so continuous-effect recalculation doesn't undo it. `power`/`toughness`\n  properties raise AttributeError until animated because state-based actions\n  key off `hasattr(obj, \"toughness\")`.\n- sos_257 (and other ability cards): the engine never consumes\n  `get_mana_abilities`/`get_activated_abilities` itself; tests drive printed\n  abilities by index by wrapping them in `ActivatedAbilityInstance` and going\n  through `engine.abilities.activate_ability` + stack resolution — the same\n  path the ability layer uses.\n- sos_257: a land played and animated the same turn would have summoning\n  sickness; not tracked (animation clears `summoning_sick`) — commented in\n  the card file.\n\"\"\")\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"sos_257: Great Hall of the Biblioplex\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Mark, log, commit sos_257"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":97