{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01TWBYtw89UUb6bwjL3msGFb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MYshvyyYiUYsPqpK9Rxarg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='TODO.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace('- [ ] **sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares**', '- [x] **sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares**')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nwith open('KEY_DECISIONS.md','a') as f:\n    f.write(\"\"\"\n- sos_13: the engine fires the enters-battlefield event *before* registering\n  the entering permanent's own triggers, so a self-ETB registration never\n  fires through the real cast path (verified: fdn_136's ETB is dead through\n  `cast_spell`). Card-local workaround: `register_triggers` (which the\n  engine calls exactly at entry) pushes the enter trigger onto the stack\n  directly.\n- sos_13: per rule 722.3c (confirmed in RULEBOOK.txt) the Swords copy is\n  created in exile when the permanent becomes *prepared* (not on elect, as\n  TODO suggested), is cast paying its normal {W} cost (not free), and\n  ceases to exist if the permanent leaves the battlefield or otherwise\n  unprepares. Electing the cast is exposed as `cast_prepared_spell(game)` —\n  no engine seam exists for player-elected casts from exile.\n- sos_13: a cast copy that resolves ends up in the owner's graveyard instead\n  of ceasing to exist (the engine has no copy-cleanup SBA) — deliberate\n  limitation.\n\"\"\")\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"sos_13: Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Mark, log, commit sos_13"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1132,"cache_read_input_tokens":259020,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1132},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"